{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionInvariantObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionInvariantObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Action.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionObstruction.exists_nonzero_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionObstruction.exists_nonzero_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionInvariantObstruction.lean#L51-L57","doc":"The fixed unit is automatic in the associative case: a group acting on a nontrivial\nsemiring by ring automorphisms fixes `1`, a nonzero invariant.  (The octonions are\nnon-associative, but their identity is fixed by any automorphism for the same reason —\n`φ(1)` is an identity, hence equal to the unique identity `1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionObstruction.no_fixed_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.OctonionObstruction.no_fixed_unit","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/OctonionInvariantObstruction.lean#L41-L49","doc":"**Invariant-vector obstruction (kernel).**  A `G`-module `A` with no nonzero\n`G`-invariant vector contains no nonzero `G`-fixed element `u`.  Since an algebra\nautomorphism fixes the identity, a unital algebra with `G` acting by automorphisms\n*does* have such a fixed unit (`u = 1 ≠ 0`); so a `G`-module with no invariant\ncannot be one.  Fully general — no associativity, so it applies to the octonions. ","signatureChunk":0}]}